From e250169eb23e2d59bfa5e6e7f87893206a7288a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mgirom <84082110+mgirom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 04:15:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] cpca: per-head multiply as one ggml_mul_mat_id, no layout
 copies; matrices f16 on device; query-side matrices per query head

The permute-and-copy helper is replaced by the expert operator with constant index
tables. The CUDA path of that operator is exercised by mixture models only with at
most as many slots as matrices, and returned garbage for 16 query heads over 8 kv
matrices while the CPU path was correct; the query-side matrices are therefore
expanded to one per query head at load (trivial memory) and the table is the
identity. The permute helper remains for reference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/llama-graph.cpp    |  8 +++---
 src/llama-impl.h       | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/llama-kv-cache.cpp | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 src/llama-kv-cache.h   |  5 ++++
 4 files changed, 88 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

